From 01f9c8a4a7fa95e8e78cbc312348462329a2e904 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LLCOOLT <114613597+LLCOOLT@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:50:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 34/36] present: copy present for Linux KMSDRM (handhelds
 without X11 or Wayland)

Dawn's OpenGL ES backend presents only to X11, Wayland and Android
windows. Linux handhelds (PortMaster on Knulli, muOS, ROCKNIX, the makers'
firmwares) often have neither: SDL3 draws straight to the screen through
KMSDRM. There the frame is drawn into a texture on SDL's own EGL display,
copied into one of two readback buffers, and the one from the frame before
is shown through SDL's OpenGL ES renderer, which flips it to the screen.

Chosen for the OpenGL ES backend when SDL's video driver is kmsdrm or
offscreen (AURORA_PRESENT=copy forces it, =surface turns it off). Vulkan
on KMSDRM still has no surface and falls through to OpenGL ES as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
